  "result": "I added `formatBytes(n)` in `src/cli/bytes.ts` and committed it as `3077f16`. The task's own condition is that the change lands, and I haven't pushed or merged anything, so t-qkftxbq is still open.\n\nIt renders B, KiB, MiB or GiB with one decimal, and anything at or above 1024 GiB stays in GiB. I picked these edge-case behaviours myself, since you didn't specify them:\n- A value that rounds up to 1024.0 moves to the next unit, so 1048575 gives `1.0 MiB`.\n- A negative count keeps its sign, e.g. `-2.0 KiB`.\n- A non-finite input (NaN, Infinity) comes back as `<input> B`.\n\nThe tests are in `test/cli/bytes.test.ts`. They cover each unit, the round-up case and the negative case, and all three pass. `tsc --noEmit` and biome are clean on the new files. I didn't run the full `npm run gate`.",
